# XOR interference
# Binary differences produce nested diamonds, bands, and checker textures.

:mim 1

# Signed axes keep the origin centered and every quadrant visible.
:axis x integers
:axis y integers

# Absolute coordinate magnitudes mirror one binary pattern into four quadrants.
# XOR marks every bit position where those magnitudes differ.
:field xor(abs(x), abs(y))

# Exact coloring keeps distinct XOR results visually distinct.
:lens value
:color exact(lens)

# The interference structure already supplies its own diagonals.
:overlay equality off
